            <description lang="en">Request to print a hexadecimal code
0 is a reserved value and cannot be printed</description>
            <UINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_OBJ_6000">
            <description lang="en">Controls and manages the connexions between tools and test points on the DAQ.

#### Available Points:

- 0: `NONE`
- 1: `MUX1_A0`
- 2: `MUX1_A1`
- 3: `MUX1_A2`
- 4: `MUX1_A3`
- 5: `MUX1_B0`
- 6: `MUX1_B1`
- 7: `MUX1_B2`
- 8: `MUX1_B3`
- 9: `MUX1_OUT`
- 10: `MUX2_A0`
- 11: `MUX2_A1`
- 12: `MUX2_A2`
- 13: `MUX2_A3`
- 14: `MUX2_B0`
- 15: `MUX2_B1`
- 16: `MUX2_B2`
- 17: `MUX2_B3`
- 18: `MUX2_OUT`
- 19: `MUX3_A0`
- 20: `MUX3_A1`
- 21: `MUX3_A2`
- 22: `MUX3_A3`
- 23: `MUX3_B0`
- 24: `MUX3_B1`
- 25: `MUX3_B2`
- 26: `MUX3_B3`
- 27: `MUX3_OUT`
- 28: `MUX4_A0`
- 29: `MUX4_A1`
- 30: `MUX4_A2`
- 31: `MUX4_A3`
- 32: `MUX4_B0`
- 33: `MUX4_B1`
- 34: `MUX4_B2`
- 35: `MUX4_B3`
- 36: `MUX4_OUT`
- 37: `MUX5_A0`
- 38: `MUX5_A1`
- 39: `MUX5_A2`
- 40: `MUX5_A3`
- 41: `MUX5_B0`
- 42: `MUX5_B1`
- 43: `MUX5_B2`
- 44: `MUX5_B3`
- 45: `MUX5_OUT`
- 46: `MUX6_A0`
- 47: `MUX6_A1`
- 48: `MUX6_A2`
- 49: `MUX6_A3`
- 50: `MUX6_B0`
- 51: `MUX6_B1`
- 52: `MUX6_B2`
- 53: `MUX6_B3`
- 54: `MUX6_OUT`
- 55: `R100_1`
- 56: `R100_2` - This is the same as `R100_1`, but is required internally.
- 57: `R4k99_1`
- 58: `R4k99_2` - This is the same as `R4k99_1`, but is required internally.
- 59: `R100k_1`
- 60: `R100k_2` - This is the same as `R100k_1`, but is required internally.
- 61: `R1M_1`
- 62: `R1M_2` - This is the same as `R1M_1`, but is required internally.
- 63: `P3V3`
- 64: `P5V`
- 65: `P2V048`
- 66: `P24V`
- 67: `GND`
- 68: `DAC`
- 69: `BUS_IO_A`
- 70: `BUS_IO_B`
- 71: `ADC_CH1`  - Corresponds to `SIG_ADC_2` in the schematics.
- 72: `ADC_CH2`  - Corresponds to `SIG_ADC_3` in the schematics.
- 73: `IMP_P`
- 74: `IMP_N`
- 75: `GUARD`
- 76: `BUS` - Debug only. Allows connecting one point to bus
</description>
            <q1:dataTypeIDRef uniqueIDRef="UID_REC_6000" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600000">
            <label lang="en">Highest sub-index supported</label>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0x0B" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600001" access="write">
            <description lang="en">#### Request Routing
Requests a connexion between two or more points (up to 14) on an available bus.

Each byte of the string correspond to a point to connect. The first point being null (set to 0) indicates the end of the list.
</description>
            <BITSTRING />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:property name="CO_stringLengthMin" value="15" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600002" access="write">
            <description lang="en">#### Clear All
Clears every active connexions on the bus.
</description>
            <BOOL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600003">
            <description lang="en">#### Bus 1 State
Current state of bus 1.

Each byte of the string correspond to a point to connect. The first point being null (set to 0) indicates the end of the list.
</description>
            <BITSTRING />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:property name="CO_stringLengthMin" value="15" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600004" access="write">
            <description lang="en">#### Clear Bus 1
Clears bus 1.

</description>
            <BOOL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600005">
            <description lang="en">#### Bus 2 State
Current state of bus 2.

Each byte of the string correspond to a point to connect. The first point being null (set to 0) indicates the end of the list.
</description>
            <BITSTRING />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:property name="CO_stringLengthMin" value="15" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600006" access="write">
            <description lang="en">#### Clear Bus 2
Clears bus 2.
</description>
            <BOOL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600007">
            <description lang="en">#### Bus 3 State
Current state of bus 3.

Each byte of the string correspond to a point to connect. The first point being null (set to 0) indicates the end of the list.
</description>
            <BITSTRING />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:property name="CO_stringLengthMin" value="15" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600008" access="write">
            <description lang="en">#### Clear Bus 3
Clears bus 3.
</description>
            <BOOL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600009">
            <description lang="en">#### Bus 4 State
Current state of bus 4.

Each byte of the string correspond to a point to connect. The first point being null (set to 0) indicates the end of the list.
</description>
            <BITSTRING />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:property name="CO_stringLengthMin" value="15" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_60000A" access="write">
            <description lang="en">#### Clear Bus 2
Clears bus 2.
</description>
            <BOOL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_60000B">
            <description lang="en">#### Last Result
Result of the last Request Routing operation.
- 0: No Action taken
- &lt;0: Error code
- &gt;0: Bus on which the signal was mapped to
</description>
            <SINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_OBJ_6001">
            <description lang="en">0-12V DAC.
Supports sine wave, triangle, sawtooth and noise, up to 300kHz.

Note: DAC output is set to 1MSP.</description>
            <q1:dataTypeIDRef uniqueIDRef="UID_REC_6001" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600100">
            <label lang="en">Highest sub-index supported</label>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0x04" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600101" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Enable
Toggles the DAC.
</description>
            <BOOL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600102" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Amplitude
Amplitude of the output signal, in volts.
When Shape is not Flat, the voltage is expressed in Volts Peak-Peak.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:allowedValues>
              <q1:range>
                <minValue value="0" />
                <maxValue value="12" />
              </q1:range>
            </q1:allowedValues>
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600103" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Frequency
Frequency of the signal, in hertz.
From 0 to 300kHz.

Note: DAC output is set to 1MSP.

</description>
            <UDINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:allowedValues>
              <q1:range>
                <minValue value="0" />
                <maxValue value="300000" />
              </q1:range>
            </q1:allowedValues>
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600104" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Shape
Shape of the output signal.

* 1: Flat
* 2: Sine
* 3: Sawtooth
* 4: Triangle
* 5: Square
* 6: Noise


</description>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:allowedValues>
              <q1:range>
                <minValue value="0" />
                <maxValue value="5" />
              </q1:range>
            </q1:allowedValues>
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_OBJ_6002">
            <description lang="en">Digital IO pins.</description>
            <q1:dataTypeIDRef uniqueIDRef="UID_REC_6002" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600200">
            <label lang="en">Highest sub-index supported</label>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0x04" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600201" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Mode
Sets the direction of the pins.

When configured in alternate mode, writing and reading to a peripheral pin does not do anything.

* 0: Input
* 1: Output

* Bit 0: Direction of BUS_IO_A,
* Bit 1: Direction of BUS_IO_B,
* Bit 2: Direction of SPI_UUT_SCK,
* Bit 3: Direction of SPI_UUT_MOSI,
* Bit 4: Direction of SPI_UUT_MISO,
* Bit 5: Direction of I2C_UUT_SCL_OUT,
* Bit 6: Direction of I2C_UUT_SDA_OUT,
* Bit 7: Direction of UART_UUT_TX,
* Bit 8: Direction of UART_UUT_RX,
* Bit 9: Direction of DB9_SPARE_IO.
</description>
            <UINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600202">
            <description lang="en">#### Input Port
Current state of the Input port of IO pins.

When configured in alternate mode, writing and reading to a pin does not do anything.

* 0: Low
* 1: High

* Bit 0: Value of BUS_IO_A,
* Bit 1: Value of BUS_IO_B,
* Bit 2: Value of SPI_UUT_SCK,
* Bit 3: Value of SPI_UUT_MOSI,
* Bit 4: Value of SPI_UUT_MISO,
* Bit 5: Value of I2C_UUT_SCL_OUT,
* Bit 6: Value of I2C_UUT_SDA_OUT,
* Bit 7: Value of UART_UUT_TX,
* Bit 8: Value of UART_UUT_RX,
* Bit 9: Value of DB9_SPARE_IO.
</description>
            <UINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600203" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Value
Current state of the Ouput port of IO pins.

When configured in alternate mode, writing and reading to a pin does not do anything.

* 0: Low
* 1: High

* Bit 0: Value of BUS_IO_A,
* Bit 1: Value of BUS_IO_B,
* Bit 2: Value of SPI_UUT_SCK,
* Bit 3: Value of SPI_UUT_MOSI,
* Bit 4: Value of SPI_UUT_MISO,
* Bit 5: Value of I2C_UUT_SCL_OUT,
* Bit 6: Value of I2C_UUT_SDA_OUT,
* Bit 7: Value of UART_UUT_TX,
* Bit 8: Value of UART_UUT_RX,
* Bit 9: Value of DB9_SPARE_IO.
</description>
            <UINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600204" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Alternate Function
Selects whether the pins of a peripheral are in GPIO mode or in their alternate function mode. 
By default, every peripherals are in GPIO mode.

* Bit 0: SPI Mode (SPI_UUT_SCK, SPI_UUT_MOSI, SPI_UUT_MISO)
  * 0: GPIO
  * 1: SPI
* Bit 1: I2C Mode (I2C_UUT_SCL_OUT, I2C_UUT_SDA_OUT)
  * 0: GPIO
  * 1: I2C
* Bit 2: UART Mode (UART_UUT_TX, UART_UUT_RX)
  * 0: GPIO
  * 1: UART</description>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_OBJ_6003">
            <description lang="en">Controls the signaling system of the DAQ.
This includes a column of LED, as well as a buzzer.
</description>
            <q1:dataTypeIDRef uniqueIDRef="UID_REC_6003" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600300">
            <label lang="en">Highest sub-index supported</label>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0x0C" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600301" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Mode
Active signal.

* 0: Off
* 1: Idle Animation (Rainbow)
* 2: Standby (Green)
* 3: Busy (Yellow)
* 4: Error/Action Required (Red)
* 5: Lock-out (Blue)
* 6: Danger Warning (Flashing red with buzzer, 1s period, 50% duty cycle)
* 7: Danger Warning Muted (Flashing red, 1s period, 50% duty cycle)
* 8: Boot (White)
* 9: Custom (The color of each LED is dictated by sub indices 4 through 12)
</description>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:allowedValues>
              <q1:range>
                <minValue value="0" />
                <maxValue value="9" />
              </q1:range>
            </q1:allowedValues>
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600302" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Mode Modifier
Applies a modifier to the currently active mode.

* 0: Off
* 1: On for 100ms every 3 seconds
* 2: On for 100ms every second
* 3: On for 250ms every second
* 4: On for 500ms every second
* 5: On for 125ms every 250ms
* 6: Strobe
</description>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:allowedValues>
              <q1:range>
                <minValue value="0" />
                <maxValue value="6" />
              </q1:range>
            </q1:allowedValues>
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600303" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Idle Time
Time (in minutes) after which the system goes back into Idle Mode.
When set to 0, the system will not go into Idle Mode.

The system will only go into idle mode if it currently is in standby mode.
To go out of idle mode, 
</description>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="5" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600304" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Buzzer Mode
Mode of the buzzer.

* Bits 0 to 7:
  * 0: Off
  * 1: On for 100ms every 3 seconds
  * 2: On for 500ms every second
  * 3: On for 900ms every second
  * 4: On for 100ms every second
  * 5: On for 125ms every 250ms
* Bits 8 to 15: Number of seconds to use the mode for.
  * 0: Disabled
  * 1 to 254: Seconds
  * 255: Always active
</description>
            <UINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="5" />
          </q1:parameter>
