          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_OBJ_600A">
            <description lang="en">Controls and reports various parts of the ADC subsystem, including the ADS131 and the internal ADC used by the STM32.

Procedure to read values from the ADC:
1. Connect a (or multiple) points to `ADC_CH1` and/or `ADC_CH2` through the `Routing` object entry
2. Set the desired `Sample Rate` and `Channel Gain`
3. Set `Samples to Take` to the desired value
4. Poll `Samples to Take` periodically until it reaches 0
5. Read the result entries
</description>
            <q1:dataTypeIDRef uniqueIDRef="UID_REC_600A" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600A00">
            <label lang="en">Highest sub-index supported</label>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0x16" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600A01">
            <description lang="en">#### ID Check
Voltage read on DB9_ID_Check. This can be used to identify the kind of UUT presently connected to the interface.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600A02" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Samples to Take
Number of samples that needs to be taken by the ADC. 

If this field is currently set to 0, setting it to anything besides 0 resets the statistics and starts the conversion.

This field is automatically decremented by the system; once it hits 0, the acquisitions have been taken and the statistics can be read.

During acquisitions, the statistics fields are not valid.
</description>
            <UINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:allowedValues>
              <q1:range>
                <minValue value="0" />
                <maxValue value="1000" />
              </q1:range>
            </q1:allowedValues>
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600A03" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Sample Rate
Rate at which samples are taken on the ADS131.

**Note**: The sample rate will only be applied when `Samples to Take` is equal to 0.

* 0: 0.250 kHz
* 1: 0.500 kHz
* 2: 1.000 kHz
* 3: 2.000 kHz
* 4: 2.560 kHz
* 5: 2.667 kHz
* 6: 4.000 kHz
* 7: 5.120 kHz
* 8: 5.333 kHz
* 9: 8.000 kHz
* 10: 10.240 kHz
* 11: 10.667 kHz
* 12: 16.000 kHz
* 13: 20.480 kHz
* 14: 21.333 kHz
* 15: 32.000 kHz
* 16: 42.667 kHz
* 17: 64.000 kHz
* 18: 85.333 kHz
* 19: 128.000 kHz
</description>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="10" />
            <q1:allowedValues>
              <q1:range>
                <minValue value="0" />
                <maxValue value="19" />
              </q1:range>
            </q1:allowedValues>
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600A04" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 1 Gain
Gain for channel 1.

**Note**: The gain will only be applied when `Samples to Take` is equal to 0.

* 0: x1
* 1: x2
* 2: x4
* 3: x8
* 4: x16
</description>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:allowedValues>
              <q1:range>
                <minValue value="0" />
                <maxValue value="4" />
              </q1:range>
            </q1:allowedValues>
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600A05" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 2 Gain
Gain for channel 2.

**Note**: The sample rate will only be applied when `Samples to Take` is equal to 0.

* 0: x1
* 1: x2
* 2: x4
* 3: x8
* 4: x16
</description>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:allowedValues>
              <q1:range>
                <minValue value="0" />
                <maxValue value="4" />
              </q1:range>
            </q1:allowedValues>
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600A06" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 3 Gain
Gain for channel 3.

**Note**: The sample rate will only be applied when `Samples to Take` is equal to 0.

* 0: x1
* 1: x2
* 2: x4
* 3: x8
* 4: x16
</description>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:allowedValues>
              <q1:range>
                <minValue value="0" />
                <maxValue value="4" />
              </q1:range>
            </q1:allowedValues>
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600A07" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 4 Gain
Gain for channel 4.

**Note**: The sample rate will only be applied when `Samples to Take` is equal to 0.

* 0: x1
* 1: x2
* 2: x4
* 3: x8
* 4: x16
</description>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:allowedValues>
              <q1:range>
                <minValue value="0" />
                <maxValue value="4" />
              </q1:range>
            </q1:allowedValues>
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600A08">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 1 Min
Lowest value read on channel 1, in volts.
Only valid when `Samples to Take` is 0.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600A09">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 1 Average
Average value read on channel 1, in volts.
Only valid when `Samples to Take` is 0.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600A0A">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 1 Max
Highest value read on channel 1, in volts.
Only valid when `Samples to Take` is 0.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600A0B">
