          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600B03">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 1 Gain 4k99
Gain of channel 1 (IMP_+) when in the 4.99 kiloohms range.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="1.0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600B04">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 2 Gain 4k99
Gain of channel 2 (IMP_-) when in the 4.99 kiloohms range.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="1.0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600B05">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 1 Gain 100k
Gain of channel 1 (IMP_+) when in the 100 kiloohms range.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="1.0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600B06">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 2 Gain 100k
Gain of channel 2 (IMP_-) when in the 100 kiloohms range.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="1.0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600B07">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 1 Gain 1M
Gain of channel 1 (IMP_+) when in the 1 megaohms range.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="1.0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600B08">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 2 Gain 1M
Gain of channel 2 (IMP_-) when in the 1 megaohms range.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="1.0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600B09">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 1 Offset 100R
Offset, in volt, of channel 1 (IMP_+) when in the 100 ohms range.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600B0A">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 2 Offset 100R
Offset, in volt, of channel 2 (IMP_-) when in the 100 ohms range.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600B0B">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 1 Offset 4k99
Offset, in volt, of channel 1 (IMP_+) when in the 4.99 kiloohms range.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600B0C">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 2 Offset 4k99
Offset, in volt, of channel 2 (IMP_-) when in the 4.99 kiloohms range.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600B0D">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 1 Offset 100k
Offset, in volt, of channel 1 (IMP_+) when in the 100 kiloohms range.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600B0E">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 2 Offset 100k
Offset, in volt, of channel 2 (IMP_-) when in the 100 kiloohms range.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600B0F">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 1 Offset 1M
Offset, in volt, of channel 1 (IMP_+) when in the 1 megaohms range.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600B10">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 2 Offset 1M
Offset, in volt, of channel 2 (IMP_-) when in the 1 megaohms range.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600B11">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 2 Gain
Gain of channel 2 (ADC_CH1).
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="1.0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600B12">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 3 Gain
Gain of channel 3 (ADC_CH2).
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="1.0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600B13">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 2 Offset
Offset, in volts, of channel 2 (ADC_CH1).
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600B14">
            <description lang="en">#### Channel 3 Offset
Offset, in volts, of channel 3 (ADC_CH2).
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_OBJ_600C">
            <description lang="en">Performs impedance measurements, allowing the user to determine the values of resistors, capacitors and inductors.

**NOTE:** Parameters must not be changed while an acquisition is in progress (`Trigger` set to 1)!

Procedure to measure an impedance:
1. Connect the point on which to inject the signal to `IMP_P` and to `ADC_CH1` through the `Routing` object. It is important to use `ADC_CH1` and not `ADC_CH2`, since the conversion algorithms assumes `ADC_CH1` to be Vout.
2. Connect the point on which to read the signal to `IMP_N` through the `Routing` object.
3. (Optional) Connect the points to be guarded to `GUARD` through the `Routing` object.
4. Set the `Mode` of impedance measurment (Resistor, Capacitor or Inductor).
5. Configure the various settings of the capture through this object.
6. Initiate the capture by setting `Trigger` to 1.
7. Poll `Trigger`, it will be set to 0 automatically when the capture is complete.
8. Read the resulting `Value`, as well as the other results fields.

If automatic settings were used, their value can be read to fetch what parameters were used by the system once the capture is complete.
</description>
            <q1:dataTypeIDRef uniqueIDRef="UID_REC_600C" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600C00">
            <label lang="en">Highest sub-index supported</label>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0x0E" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600C01" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Trigger
Set by software, cleared by hardware.

When set to 1, the capture process is started using the given parameters. 
If any parameters were set to Automatic, they are calculated before starting.

Once the capture is complete, the hardware sets this field to 0.

The values of `Confidence`, `Value`, `Vin` and `Vout` are undefined for as long as this bit is set.
</description>
            <BOOL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:allowedValues>
              <q1:range>
                <minValue value="false" />
                <maxValue value="true" />
              </q1:range>
            </q1:allowedValues>
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600C02" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Mode
Mode of capture.

* 0: Resistor
* 1: Capacitor
* 2: Inductor
</description>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:allowedValues>
              <q1:range>
                <minValue value="0" />
                <maxValue value="2" />
              </q1:range>
            </q1:allowedValues>
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600C03" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Shape
Shape of the signal that will be injected into the part to be measured.

* 0: Automatic
* 1: Flat
* 2: Sine
* 3: Sawtooth
* 4: Triangle
* 5: Square
* 6: Noise
</description>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:allowedValues>
              <q1:range>
                <minValue value="0" />
                <maxValue value="6" />
              </q1:range>
            </q1:allowedValues>
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600C04" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Range Resistor
Range resistor to use during the measurment. 

Ideally, you will want to use the range that is the closest to the impedance you are trying to measure. This is however not universal.

* 0: Automatic
* 1: 100 Ohms
* 2: 4.99 kiloohms
* 3: 100 kiloohms
* 4: 1 megaohm</description>
            <USINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:allowedValues>
              <q1:range>
                <minValue value="0" />
                <maxValue value="4" />
              </q1:range>
            </q1:allowedValues>
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600C05" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Frequency
Frequency of the injected signal.

When `Shape` is set to `DC`, this value is unused.

Set to 0 if this parameter should be deduced automatically.
</description>
            <UINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:allowedValues>
              <q1:range>
                <minValue value="0" />
                <maxValue value="10000" />
              </q1:range>
            </q1:allowedValues>
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600C06" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Amplitude
Amplitude of the injected signal, in volts. 

If `Shape` is not set to `DC`, this value corresponds to the peak to peak voltage of the signal.
The available range in that case is from 0V to 3.3V.

If `Shape` is set to `DC`, the available range is from -1.65V to 1.65V.

Set to 0 if this parameter should take a default value of 100mV.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:allowedValues>
              <q1:range>
                <minValue value="-1.65" />
                <maxValue value="3.3" />
              </q1:range>
            </q1:allowedValues>
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600C07" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Delay
Delay between the injection of the signal and the beginning of the capture, expressed in microseconds.

In reality, this delay will be expressed as a number of samples that will be ignored, with a minimum of 1 sample.

Set to 0 if this parameter should take a default value of 12us.
</description>
            <UDINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600C08" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Samples to Take
Number of samples to take. 

If 0, 3 cycles of the injected frequency will be taken if Shape is not DC. 
Otherwise, 3 samples are taken.
</description>
            <UDINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
            <q1:allowedValues>
              <q1:range>
                <minValue value="0" />
                <maxValue value="1000" />
              </q1:range>
            </q1:allowedValues>
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600C09" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Expected Value
Value that is expected to be read during the capture.
This field is mandatory if either `Range Resistor` or `Frequency` (or both) are set to be determined automatically.

The unit depends on the value of `Mode`:
- `Mode` `Resistor`: ohms
- `Mode` `Capacitor`: pico farads
- `Mode` `Inductor`: micro henry
</description>
            <UDINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600C0A" access="readWrite">
            <description lang="en">#### Favor Speed
When enabled, the system will perform the capture as fast as possible. This means that only one capture will effectively be done.

When disabled (by default), the system will perform as many captures (up to 5) until it reaches a threshold of confidence in the results acquired.
</description>
            <BOOL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600C0B">
            <description lang="en">#### Confidence
Level of confidence in the value read in relation to the given parameters.

This value ranges from -100 to +100.
 * A value that tends towards -100 indicates an impedance below the selected range.
 * A value that tends towards 100 indicates an impedance above the selected range.
 * A value of 0 indicates an impedance perfectly matching the selected range.

The value is undefined (shouldn't be read) when `Trigger` is set to 1.
</description>
            <SINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600C0C">
            <description lang="en">#### Value
Value of the part measured, in Ohms, pF or uH, based on `Mode`.

The value is undefined (shouldn't be read) when `Trigger` is set to 1.
</description>
            <UDINT />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600C0D">
            <description lang="en">#### Vin
Voltage read on the injection side of the part.

The value is undefined (shouldn't be read) when `Trigger` is set to 1.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
          <q1:parameter uniqueID="UID_SUB_600C0E">
            <description lang="en">#### Vout
Voltage read on the reading side of the part.

The value is undefined (shouldn't be read) when `Trigger` is set to 1.
</description>
            <REAL />
            <q1:defaultValue value="0" />
          </q1:parameter>
        </q1:parameterList>
      </q1:ApplicationProcess>
    </ProfileBody>
  </ISO15745Profile>
